.TH UNALZ 1 "2026-07-29" "unalz 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unalz \- extract or list an ALZ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unalz
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIARCHIVE\fR [\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
.B unalz
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fB\-\fR [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unalz
extracts or lists the contents of an ALZ archive. With no \fIFILE\fR operand,
every entry is extracted; otherwise only the named entries are. A lone
.B \-
in place of \fIARCHIVE\fR reads the archive from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List archive contents instead of extracting.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-output\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Extract into \fIDIR\fR (default: the current directory).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pipe
Extract to standard output instead of to files.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password " \fIPW\fR"
Decryption password for an encrypted archive. When omitted, an encrypted
archive prompts on the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress progress messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.PP
Short flags may be bundled, for example
.BR \-lq .
An option that takes an argument may be given as
.BR \-d DIR ", " "\-d " DIR ", " \-\-output\-dir=DIR ", or " "\-\-output\-dir " DIR.
A
.B \-\-
argument ends option parsing; every argument after it is treated as a
\fIFILE\fR name.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Everything was extracted.
.TP
.B 1
Extracted every complete file, but the archive was truncated (a missing volume
or an interrupted download).
.TP
.B 2
A fatal error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B unalz archive.alz
Extract every file into the current directory.
.TP
.B unalz \-d out/ \-P secret archive.alz
Extract an encrypted archive into \fBout/\fR.
.TP
.B unalz \-l archive.alz
List the archive contents.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR unegg (1)
